{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Fools</b> — He also mentioned that illness is because of transgression, and rebukes for iniquity, and so too in the words of Elihu." "And the meaning of <b>fools</b> — even if they are wise, they are reckoned as fools because of their transgression." "And the word מדרך — draws itself and another with it, and thus it is: וּמִדְרָךְ עֲו‍ֹנֹתֵיהֶם יִתְעַנּוּ (and by the path of their iniquities they shall be afflicted)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:58.765149051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}